      "description": "Two-loop sunset graph with three internal propagators, one of which carries mass $m$, and external momentum $p$. The paper defines a seven-argument integral family $I(m^2,p^2,\\nu_1,\\ldots,\\nu_5,D)$ with two irreducible numerators $(k+l)^2$ and $(k+p)^2$, chooses two masters $I^{(1)} = (p^2-m^2) I(m^2,p^2,1,1,1,0,0,2-2\\varepsilon)$ and $I^{(2)} = -I(m^2,p^2,1,1,1,1,0,2-2\\varepsilon)$, both evaluated in closed form as Gauss ${}_2F_1$ hypergeometric functions of $p^2/m^2$. The maximal cuts are computed by iterated residues / dispersion-like frame parametrization and give two distinct cut contours (second ${}_2F_1$ arguments $1-m^2/p^2$ and $p^2/(p^2-m^2)$); the diagrammatic coaction $\\Delta I^{(i)} = \\sum_j I^{(j)} \\otimes C^{(j)} I^{(i)}$ is established.",
